      "text": [
        " اَلرَّجُلِ يَشْتَرِي اَلْمَتَاعَ جَمِيعاً بِثَمَنٍ ثُمَّ يُقَوِّمُ كُلَّ ثَوْبٍ بِمَا يَسْوَى حَتَّى يَقَعَ عَلَى رَأْسِ مَالِهِ يَبِيعُهُ مُرَابَحَةً ثَوْباً ثَوْباً قَالَ \"لاَ حَتَّى يُبَيِّنَ لَهُ أَنَّهُ إِنَّمَا قَوَّمَهُ \"."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.bab-ul-qaim-publications": [
          "Hadith.3801 - Al-'Ala narrated from Muhammad ibn Muslim, from one of the Imams (as), regarding a man who purchases goods altogether for a set price and then appraises each garment based on its value until it equals his capital, selling it item by item at a profit\nImam (as) said: \"No, not until he clarifies to the buyer that he merely appraised it.\""
        ]
      }
